        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Proof. Let  $ G = BL_n(k-1, k) $ and  $ [n] = \\{1, 2, \\ldots, n\\} $. Recall that  $ V(G) = V_1 \\cup V_2 $, where",
            "block_bbox": [
                160,
                382,
                1015,
                439
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    160.0,
                    382.0
                ],
                [
                    1015.0,
                    382.0
                ],
                [
                    1015.0,
                    439.0
                ],
                [
                    160.0,
                    439.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ V_{1}=\\{U\\subset[n]\\mid|U|=k-1\\},\\quad|V_{1}|=\\binom{n}{k-1}, $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                340,
                436,
                840,
                492
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
